WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.060
Proposition one asks whether California should borrow money

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:04.800
for housing.

3
00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:08.567
This measure authorizes eleven point two five billion

4
00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:12.142
dollars: ten billion for housing programs, and one

5
00:00:12.142 --> 00:00:15.187
point two five billion for veterans’ home loans.

6
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.880
The General Fund would repay the housing portion

7
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.680
at about five hundred to six hundred million

8
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.720
dollars a year for roughly twenty-five years.

9
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.920
Veterans’ loan payments would repay their separate bond

10
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.420
portion.

11
00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:31.153
A voter might support financing affordable homes sooner

12
00:00:31.153 --> 00:00:34.313
rather than waiting for enough money in annual

13
00:00:34.313 --> 00:00:34.633
budgets.

14
00:00:34.953 --> 00:00:38.073
Interest adds expense, and future repayments compete with

15
00:00:38.073 --> 00:00:38.793
other services.

16
00:00:39.093 --> 00:00:40.813
Yes authorizes this borrowing;

17
00:00:41.613 --> 00:00:44.973
no rejects this bond, while existing housing programs

18
00:00:44.973 --> 00:00:45.693
continue.

19
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.400
Visit our website for the fuller explanation, source

20
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.520
links, and official voter guide.
